{"title":"2017 EGMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20db01d8f52491da1351b381236e238622cdcb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB=\\angle BCD=90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"186\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0969976c3afaf20d93e6e1b14b30a47418f26c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC&gt; \\angle CDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be points on segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, such that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> intersects lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. It is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4d3cec6c92bfcb4eea6e657f6b27a7655f238a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=RS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />.Let the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.Prove that the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f70bb850b7dd5549e8955bc5dfea63d64243a9cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M,N,A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle.\t\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 EGMO Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which there exists a colouring of the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/16172fdaef5fff0016ff1656660f8d7f6ba21d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> colours and a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9cdf1c4aaf80ec8f956f6ea2f07bc3c332fc007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}\\to \\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> with the following two properties:\n</p><p><br />\n(i) For all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46ba6ed097cc88ded349bf99eea89817f135f470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> of the same colour, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3a5b1ff7c5f35e07f9c41b3d253ee1d3c94af2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m+n)=f(m)+f(n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(ii) There are positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46ba6ed097cc88ded349bf99eea89817f135f470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5d8e2f4119aaf51d15840dac87d9879be39110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m+n)\\ne f(m)+f(n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIn a colouring of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/1/16172fdaef5fff0016ff1656660f8d7f6ba21d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> colours, every integer is coloured in exactly one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> colours. In both (i) and (ii) the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46ba6ed097cc88ded349bf99eea89817f135f470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> are not necessarily distinct.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 EGMO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5617f6d8def6056c5921630439d64b56cfa519ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> lines in the plane such that no three of them go through the same point. Turbo the snail sits on a point on exactly one of the lines and starts sliding along the lines in the following fashion: she moves on a given line until she reaches an intersection of two lines. At the intersection, she follows her journey on the other line turning left or right, alternating her choice at each intersection point she reaches. She can only change direction at an intersection point. Can there exist a line segment through which she passes in both directions during her journey?\t\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 EGMO Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28324eb1d52d541982598613d2d7ac4cb4e526e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cff89851baad185b96514d11a2e2b4b36a4d597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1&lt;t_2&lt;\\dots&lt;t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" /> be positive integers. In a group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/9795df69bc2c4b031fb8b67d1ccf3966a7290dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> people, some games of chess are played. Two people can play each other at most once. Prove that it is possible for the following two conditions to hold at the same time:\n</p><p>(i) The number of games played by each person is one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0b4c923bf4393dfd9e5af0b40f9e12bb5e525c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1,t_2,\\dots,t_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>(ii) For every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20dc85bf0e34f8d7fbf66b886eedf3bee98aca45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, there is someone who has played exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273e0046b505d99f3d1167caa82b2ac76c96d075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games of chess.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 EGMO Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e4d230e75b3cb7fea5c98643fef4b6e775aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer. An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-tuple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65bdda1c8878ae099a8cce8d5a46aa7b62d87133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> of not necessarily different positive integers is expensive if there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/6/0c697ef39b2c128bb00f5160cb26da238488a847.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1+a_2)(a_2+a_3)\\dots(a_{n-1}+a_n)(a_n+a_1)=2^{2k-1}.\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"20\" />\n(a) Find all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e4d230e75b3cb7fea5c98643fef4b6e775aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> for which there exists an expensive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-tuple.\n</p><p>(b) Prove that for every odd positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4e4d230e75b3cb7fea5c98643fef4b6e775aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> belongs to an expensive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-tuple.\n</p><p>There are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> factors in the product on the left hand side.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 EGMO Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute-angled triangle in which no two sides have the same length. The reflections of the centroid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the circumcentre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> in its sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2af80f0680f9428356964113ca9e3dd3577f324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,CA,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> are denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/145408d2bb915f7535807bb40702d239904bd67c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_1,G_2,G_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee0bd0f8b301eae6e83325530771834a86d82f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1,O_2,O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />, respectively. Show that the circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdf7d5c7146bb86ac5f9bff9a181315df1e04a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_1G_2C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/0914ff1bb041e37829e225cea9a4276e96df3987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_1G_3B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2cae00a6193ea63132bfa733ab88dcfb836a858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G_2G_3A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc828474e16bef52bb166b17c136b948581158c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_2C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a255410c17fd3bd5c5d5abea2823db33107eb25a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1O_3B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c079c57b0023270a89af5511631f749e699530a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2O_3A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> have a common point.\n</p><p>The centroid of a triangle is the intersection point of the three medians. A median is a line connecting a vertex of the triangle to the midpoint of the opposite side.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_EGMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 EGMO Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061614\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 325/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11486/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23585:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018061614 and revision id 184648. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}